# Feature branch for the whole conversation

When planning or starting work, create a feature branch **once at the start** so all edits in this conversation happen on that branch.

1. Run `git branch --show-current`. If the branch is `main`, `master`, or the repo default, create and switch to a new branch (e.g. `feature/short-description`, `fix/issue-name`) with `git checkout -b <name>`.
2. Do all requested planning and code changes on this branch for the rest of the conversation. Do not create another branch mid-conversation unless the user asks.
3. If the user is already on a feature branch, stay on it and proceed without creating a new branch.